    "https://stnorbert.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/SNC_Careers/job/De-Pere-Wisconsin/Maintenance-Specialist-Locksmith_JR102022": {
      "title": "Maintenance Specialist - part-time",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nPart time\n\nSt. Norbert College (SNC), a nationally ranked, private, Catholic, liberal arts college, is seeking a part-time Maintenance Specialist to join our facilities team. The hours for this position are flexible, with a schedule of four hours per day, Monday through Friday. The position is generally not expected to work nights or weekends except for possible snow removal. Specific responsibilities: Perform numerous maintenance tasks throughout the campus, such as daily work orders, repairs, and modifications. Perform various masonry tasks and repairs. Repair broken windows and install new window components. Perform various carpentry tasks. Assist with HVAC, electrical, and plumbing repairs. Assist with snow removal and participate in the on-call program. Perform additional duties as assigned. Required Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent. 5 years of related work experience. Valid Driver’s License. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment. Strong interpersonal and conflict-resolution skills. Ability to multitask, prioritize, and meet deadlines. Basic math skills. Sound judgment and timely decision-making skills. Ability to lead by example. Ability to maintain focus in a noisy environment. The College may consider any equivalent amount of credentials, licensures, training, or experience that provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the duties and responsibilities of this job. Application instructions: This position will be posted for a minimum of five business days, and applications will be reviewed upon receipt. St. Norbert College (SNC), a Catholic, Norbertine, and Liberal Arts College, provides an educational environment that fosters intellectual, spiritual, and personal development.  As the only Norbertine institution of higher learning in the world, our roots, traditions, and commitments create a unique and enriching educational experience for our students.   At SNC, our commitment to communio – the Norbertine ideal of a community united as one – is grounded in the principles of dignity, truth, and justice. Consistent with these principles, St. Norbert is proud to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment.   We seek those who will embrace our mission and commitment to building a vibrant, inclusive, and spiritually engaged community ( https://snc.edu/mission ).   Non-Exempt Scheduled Weekly Hours: 20 The duties and responsibilities listed in this job description are intended to describe the general nature and level of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the job if work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the job. Percentage of time may vary widely depending on the needs of the position during any particular time period. This job description does not constitute an employment agreement between the employer and employee and is subject to change by the employer as the needs of the employer and requirements of the job change."
