    "https://stnorbert.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/SNC_Careers/job/De-Pere-Wisconsin/Financial-Controller_JR102062": {
      "title": "Financial Controller",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nSt. Norbert College (SNC), a nationally ranked, private, Catholic, liberal arts college, is seeking a Financial Controller. This is an on-site position requiring regular attendance on campus. The role is responsible for overseeing the College’s financial reporting, accounts receivable and payable functions, the development and maintenance of internal control systems, and the execution of internal audits. The Financial Controller plays a critical role in ensuring fiscal accountability, regulatory compliance, and operational excellence across accounting, student accounts, and internal control functions. Specific responsibilities: Establishes and monitors the internal control framework; documents key processes and performs internal audits Prepares and maintains timely, accurate financial reports (annual, quarterly, monthly, compliance, and expenditure reports) Ensures compliance with GAAP and oversees implementation of GASB pronouncements Coordinates audits, including preparation of documentation for government, Board, and external auditors; manages audit resolution and maintains audit trails Develops cash flow projections and optimizes investment strategies Reviews capital lease documents and prepares financial lease calculations Reviews outstanding purchase orders to manage surplus/deficit impact Researches and interprets Federal, State, and Board policies; stays current on higher education regulatory changes Reports on internal audit findings, recommends corrective actions, and provides staff training on internal control standards Analyzes financial data for anomalies and non-compliance; conducts follow-up reviews to ensure effective controls Performs other duties as assigned Supervision Exercised Over: Accounting Manager Director of Student Account Services Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Accounting or a related field Licensed CPA Audit or forensic accounting experience Supervisory experience Experience in Higher Education or a complex non-profit organization Knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP) and Governmental Accounting Standards Board (GASB) guidelines Knowledge of federal compliance requirements Knowledge of higher education finance and accounting practices Knowledge of computers and high efficiency in job-related software programs (Banner, Workday, Excel, financial reporting tools) Strong attention to detail and accuracy Effective organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills Clear and effective oral and written communication skills Ability to present complex financial information clearly Ability to manage competing priorities and meet tight deadlines Maintains accurate work under pressure in a demanding environment Communicates regularly on strategic matters and significant issues Demonstrates mission alignment with a student-first professional mindset The College may consider any equivalent amount of credentials, licensures, training, or experience that provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the duties and responsibilities of this job. Benefits package: The College offers an outstanding benefits package including health, dental, vision and life insurance; retirement plan; paid time-off and tuition waiver. Application instructions: Applications received by  November 13, 2026, will be given full consideration. However, applications will continue to be accepted until the position has been filled. Please submit a cover letter and resume with your application. Applicants are also required to submit a letter describing how their professional experience, leadership approach, and personal qualities align with the mission and values of St. Norbert College. This letter should address how the candidate would actively advance the Catholic, Liberal Arts, and Norbertine traditions in the context of this role. Mission alignment will be considered a significant factor in the evaluation process.   St. Norbert College (SNC), a Catholic, Norbertine, and Liberal Arts College, provides an educational environment that fosters intellectual, spiritual, and personal development.  As the only Norbertine institution of higher learning in the world, our roots, traditions, and commitments create a unique and enriching educational experience for our students.   At SNC, our commitment to communio – the Norbertine ideal of a community united as one – is grounded in the principles of dignity, truth, and justice. Consistent with these principles, St. Norbert is proud to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment.   We seek those who will embrace our mission and commitment to building a vibrant, inclusive, and spiritually engaged community ( https://snc.edu/mission ).   Exempt Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 The duties and responsibilities listed in this job description are intended to describe the general nature and level of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the job if work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the job. Percentage of time may vary widely depending on the needs of the position during any particular time period. This job description does not constitute an employment agreement between the employer and employee and is subject to change by the employer as the needs of the employer and requirements of the job change."
    },
    "https://stnorbert.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/SNC_Careers/job/De-Pere-Wisconsin/Dean-of-Faculty-Chief-Academic-Officer_JR102063-1": {
      "title": "Dean of Faculty/Chief Academic Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nSt. Norbert College seeks a mission-driven and entrepreneurial academic leader to serve as its Dean of Faculty / Chief Academic Officer. Reporting to President Laurie M. Joyner, Ph.D., and serving on the President’s Cabinet, the Dean is the College’s senior academic leader and the President’s lead partner in advancing the academic enterprise. This is a role for a change agent. The Dean will lead faculty and staff in executing a compelling value proposition for traditional undergraduates while diversifying programs and markets, including dual enrollment, online learning and lifelong learning, and will use data to guide decisions about programs, curriculum and resources. The Dean oversees an Assistant Dean of Faculty, divisional chairs, the Registrar’s Office, and the Mulva Library. Key Responsibilities Recruit, develop and evaluate faculty, including fair, rigorous evaluation and peer review for rank and promotion Steward the curriculum and academic portfolio, including launching new programs and ongoing program review using data on outcomes, demand and cost Lead assessment and accreditation, sustaining a culture of assessment and compliance with the Higher Learning Commission Manage the academic budget in line with the strategic plan, including faculty workload analysis Partner with faculty governance with candor, transparency and respect, while making and carrying out difficult decisions Advance the Catholic and Norbertine mission across teaching, scholarship and the student experience Serve as a trusted strategic partner to the President and work closely with Cabinet colleagues on enrollment, student success and financial sustainability Qualifications Earned doctorate or other terminal degree Considerable experience as a tenured faculty member, preferably at senior rank, with a record of scholarship and teaching excellence Proven academic leadership that advanced consequential outcomes for the institution An entrepreneurial record of launching or growing academic programs, partnerships or new delivery models, including hybrid learning Comfort using data to drive decisions, and experience with accreditation, strategic planning and academic budgeting A collaborative style, respect for shared governance, and the ability to lead through change A deep commitment to the Catholic and Norbertine identity of the College; a candidate deeply rooted in the Catholic faith is strongly preferred About St. Norbert College Founded in 1898 by the Norbertine order, St. Norbert College is a Catholic liberal arts college of nearly 1,400 students on 111 acres along the Fox River in De Pere, Wisconsin, just south of Green Bay. It is the only Norbertine college in the world. Guided by its motto, Docere Verbo et Exemplo (\"to teach by word and example\"), St. Norbert fosters the intellectual, spiritual and personal development of every student. The College is building on renewed momentum: three consecutive years of positive operating results, eight new majors and a 4+1 MBA launched in fall 2026, and a $15 million gift from the Norbertine community. St. Norbert is recognized by Colleges of Distinction, Niche and The Princeton Review, and 99% of students receive financial aid. Compensation and Benefits St. Norbert College offers a competitive salary commensurate with experience and a comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, and vision coverage; a 403(b) retirement plan with college match; and tuition benefits for employees, spouses, and dependents. Reasonable relocation support is available, and the successful candidate is expected to relocate to the De Pere area. How to Apply Small College Consulting is assisting St. Norbert College in this national search. Applications, nominations, and confidential inquiries may be directed to Hannah Askew at hannah@channelmarkerhr.com . Applications should include a letter of interest, a current CV, and five professional references (references will not be contacted without the candidate’s permission). Applicants are also required to submit a letter describing how their professional experience, leadership approach, and personal qualities align with the mission and values of St. Norbert College. This letter should address how the candidate would actively advance the Catholic, Liberal Arts, and Norbertine traditions in the context of this role. Mission alignment will be considered a significant factor in the evaluation process.   For full consideration, materials should be received by November 9, 2026 . Review will continue until the position is filled. The full position profile is available upon request. St. Norbert College (SNC), a Catholic, Norbertine, and Liberal Arts College, provides an educational environment that fosters intellectual, spiritual, and personal development.  As the only Norbertine institution of higher learning in the world, our roots, traditions, and commitments create a unique and enriching educational experience for our students.   At SNC, our commitment to communio – the Norbertine ideal of a community united as one – is grounded in the principles of dignity, truth, and justice. Consistent with these principles, St. Norbert is proud to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment.   We seek those who will embrace our mission and commitment to building a vibrant, inclusive, and spiritually engaged community ( https://snc.edu/mission ).   Exempt Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 The duties and responsibilities listed in this job description are intended to describe the general nature and level of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the job if work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the job. Percentage of time may vary widely depending on the needs of the position during any particular time period. This job description does not constitute an employment agreement between the employer and employee and is subject to change by the employer as the needs of the employer and requirements of the job change."
    },
    "https://stnorbert.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/SNC_Careers/job/De-Pere-Wisconsin/Financial-Aid-Counselor---Federal-Aid_JR102058": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nSt. Norbert College (SNC), a nationally ranked, private, Catholic, liberal arts college, invites applications for a Financial Aid Counselor to make a meaningful impact on students’ educational journeys. In this role, you’ll help students and families navigate the financial aid process, provide personalized guidance, and support access to higher education through the awarding of financial aid. You’ll also play an important role in ensuring compliance with federal, state, and institutional policies and regulations. This is an on-site position that requires regular attendance on campus. Specific responsibilities: Counsel prospective and continuing students and their families on financial aid eligibility and the application process, including available aid programs, educational costs, financing options, and outside scholarship opportunities. Review FAFSA applications and supporting documentation, including tax forms and schedules, to verify accuracy, identify conflicting information, interpret applicable federal regulations, and resolve discrepancies in accordance with established guidelines. Determine eligibility for and award federal, state, and institutional financial aid to undergraduate and graduate students in compliance with applicable policies and regulations. Administer federal, state, and private financial aid and scholarship programs, including loans, grants, Federal Work-Study, and state aid. Ensure timely and accurate disbursement of funds, certify loans, submit state aid vouchers, and reconcile accounts with federal and state agencies in accordance with applicable requirements. Represent the college at on- and off-campus financial aid events by developing informational materials, preparing presentations, and presenting to students, families, and other audiences. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferred in a related field. Minimum of 1 year of financial aid experience required. Banner database experience is a plus. Knowledge of federal, state, and institutional policies and regulations is preferred. Ability to work efficiently in a fast-paced environment while multitasking and meeting deadlines. Strong interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills, including conflict resolution. Proficiency in basic math and computer applications (Microsoft Office, Google Apps, Workday), with the ability to learn new systems. Strong organizational, prioritization, and project management skills, including planning events and programs through completion. Sound judgment and timely decision-making. Ability to lead by example and serve as a positive role model. Experience delivering presentations to large groups. Benefits package: The College offers an outstanding benefits package including health, dental, vision, and life insurance; retirement plan; paid time off and tuition waiver. Application instructions: Applications received by  November 6, 2026  will be given full consideration. However, applications will continue to be accepted until the position has been filled.  Please submit a cover letter and resume with your application. St. Norbert College (SNC), a Catholic, Norbertine and Liberal Arts College, provides an educational environment that fosters intellectual, spiritual and personal development.  As the only Norbertine institution of higher learning in the world, our roots, traditions, and commitments create a unique and enriching educational experience for our students.   At SNC, our commitment to  communio  – the Norbertine ideal of a community united as one – is grounded in the principles of dignity, truth and justice. Consistent with these principles, St. Norbert is proud to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment.   We seek those who will embrace our mission and commitment to building a vibrant, inclusive, and spiritually engaged community ( https://www.snc.edu/mission/gettingtoknow.html ).   Exempt Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 The duties and responsibilities listed in this job description are intended to describe the general nature and level of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the job if work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the job. Percentage of time may vary widely depending on the needs of the position during any particular time period. This job description does not constitute an employment agreement between the employer and employee and is subject to change by the employer as the needs of the employer and requirements of the job change."
    }
